{"timestamp":1774313462295,"source_app":"agentic-harness","session_id":"ece63899-cf41-4f9a-a02f-eed997ed877f","hook_event_type":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01LZgXF2erPdNXKgCjutBDJB","payload":{"session_id":"ece63899-cf41-4f9a-a02f-eed997ed877f","transcript_path":"/Users/rivero/.claude/projects/-Users-rivero-ai-agentic-experience-apps-mas-trees-18aa1878/ece63899-cf41-4f9a-a02f-eed997ed877f.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/18aa1878","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/18aa1878/specs/issue-18aa1878-adw-1-sdlc_planner-add-jsdoc-to-debounce.md","content":"# Plan: chore: add JSDoc to debounce utility in utils.js\n\n## Task Description\nThe `debounce` function in `web-components/src/utils.js` is missing a JSDoc comment block. Other exported utilities in the same file \u2014 `createTag`, `isMobileOrTablet`, `discoverService`, `paramsToHash` \u2014 already have JSDoc. Adding a matching block to `debounce` restores consistency and helps contributors understand its parameters and return type.\n\nNo functional changes are required.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `web-components/src/utils.js` \u2014 contains the `debounce` function to annotate (line 5)\n\n## Step by Step Tasks\n\n### 1. Add JSDoc block to `debounce`\n- Insert a JSDoc comment immediately above `export function debounce(func, delay)` matching the style of `createTag`\n- Document `@param {Function} func` \u2014 the function to debounce\n- Document `@param {number} delay` \u2014 delay in milliseconds\n- Document `@returns {Function}` \u2014 the debounced wrapper function\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- `debounce` in `web-components/src/utils.js` has a JSDoc block with `@param` and `@returns` tags matching the style of `createTag`\n- No functional changes to the implementation\n- `node --check web-components/src/utils.js` passes\n\n## Validation Commands\n- `node --check web-components/src/utils.js`\n"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LZgXF2erPdNXKgCjutBDJB"}}
